> API and interpretation

Only nonnegative finite decimal literals, binary + - * / ^ and parentheses
belong to the infix grammar. Negative intermediate values are supported; unary
signs and scientific literals are not. Standalone RPN also permits signed
decimals. Empty input, extra operands, missing operands, unknown characters,
unmatched brackets, zero division and nonfinite arithmetic fail explicitly.
Conversion alone accepts a syntactically valid zero divisor because it does not
evaluate.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

